---
title: The Overview page
description: See all your bots at a glance, open an account for its figures, logs and runs, and start, stop, add or remove game accounts.
appRoute: /
---

Welcome to your war room. The {% ui key="client:dashboard.title" /%} page opens when you sign in. It shows how every bot is doing, and you manage your {% term id="game-account" %}game accounts{% /term %} from here.

{% terms_on_page /%}

## The figures at the top {% #figures %}

A row of tiles sums up all your accounts:

- {% ui key="client:dashboard.stats.accounts" /%}: how many game accounts you have added.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.stats.online" /%}: how many bots are running right now.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.kpi.attacks" /%}: the attacks your bots sent in the last 24 hours.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.kpi.errors" /%}: the error lines of the last 7 days.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.kpi.coins" /%} and {% ui key="client:dashboard.kpi.rubies" /%}: the total from each account's last report.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.stats.attention" /%}: accounts that stopped and need you, such as a ban or a wrong password.

{% screenshot id="overview" alt="The Overview page: tiles for accounts, accounts online, attacks, errors, coins, rubies and accounts that need attention, then the Top accounts table." /%}

{% aside type="note" id="counted-from-logs" %}
Attacks and errors are counted from the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} lines GGE Command keeps for each account: the newest 500, and none older than 7 days. A plus after a number means some lines may have been dropped, so the real figure is at least that. Lines the game said "{% term id="not-now" %}not now{% /term %}" to are not errors.
{% /aside %}

A dash in a tile means no account has reported that figure yet. If the counts fail to load, they try again within a minute.

## Top accounts {% #top-accounts %}

With more than one account, {% ui key="client:dashboard.top.title" /%} lists the five accounts that attacked most in the last 24 hours. Each row shows the attacks, the errors and the account's status. Select a name to open that account. An account that sent no attacks is not listed.

## The roster {% #roster %}

The {% ui key="client:dashboard.roster" /%} lists every account, 20 to a page. Each row shows:

- {% ui key="client:dashboard.col.account" /%}: the name and the {% term id="server" %}server{% /term %}. An {% term id="event-twin" %}event account{% /term %} also says **event**.
- {% ui key="common:field.status" /%}: what the bot is doing now.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.col.plugins" /%}: how many {% term id="plugin" %}plugins{% /term %} are on.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.col.lastSeen" /%}: when the bot last reported. Hover for the exact time.

The buttons at the end of each row are {% ui key="common:action.start" /%} or {% ui key="common:action.stop" /%}, **Add event twin** (the lightning bolt), account settings (the gear) and edit (the pencil).

### What each status means {% #status %}

- {% ui key="ui:status.running" /%}: the bot is signed in and working.
- {% ui key="ui:status.starting" /%}: the bot is signing in. Bots start one after another, so this can take a short while.
- {% ui key="ui:status.stopped" /%}: the bot is off until you start it.
- {% ui key="ui:status.auth_failed" /%}: the game refused to let the bot sign in. See [wrong game password](/troubleshooting/#wrong-password).
- {% ui key="ui:status.banned" /%}: the game banned the account. See [banned](/troubleshooting/#banned).
- {% ui key="ui:status.error" /%}: something went wrong. Hover over the status to read the last error.
- {% ui key="ui:status.crash_loop" /%}: the bot failed again and again, so GGE Command stopped trying. This is a {% term id="crash-loop" %}crash loop{% /term %}.
- **Sleeping until Tue 08:07**: the bot is started, but it waits for the next window of its {% term id="run-schedule" %}schedule{% /term %}. The time is your own.
- {% ui key="client:dashboard.overPlan" /%}: you have more accounts than you can run, so this one cannot start. Hover for the reason.

## Start and stop a bot {% #start-stop %}

Choose {% ui key="common:action.start" /%} on the row. The bot signs in and the status changes to {% ui key="ui:status.running" /%}. Choose {% ui key="common:action.stop" /%} to end the {% term id="run" %}bot run{% /term %}. A stopped bot stays stopped until you start it again.

To act on several accounts at once, tick the box at the start of each row. The box in the header ticks every account on the page. Buttons for {% ui key="common:action.start" /%}, {% ui key="common:action.stop" /%} and {% ui key="common:action.remove" /%} appear above the roster.

## Add a game account {% #add-account %}

Choose {% ui key="client:account.add" /%} at the top of the page. The {% ui key="client:drawer.titleNew" /%} panel opens. The [quick start](/quick-start/#add-account) walks you through each field.

{% screenshot id="add-account" alt="The Add game account panel with the account name, server and game password fields, the External event account switch and the list of plugins." /%}

Some events run on a temporary event server. To play one, choose **Add event twin** on the account's row. The new account copies the name and the server, and {% ui key="client:drawer.eventLabel" /%} is already on. Event twins do not count toward the number of bots you can run.

## Open an account {% #account-drawer %}

Choose the pencil on a row, or the account's name in {% ui key="client:dashboard.top.title" /%}. A panel opens with six tabs.

- {% ui key="client:drawer.overview" /%}: six tiles with what the bot last read from the game: {% ui key="client:overview.figure.cash" /%}, {% ui key="client:overview.figure.gold" /%}, {% ui key="client:overview.figure.food" /%}, {% ui key="client:overview.figure.mead" /%}, {% ui key="client:overview.figure.aquamarine" /%} and {% ui key="client:overview.figure.attackDailyCount" /%}. Food, {% term id="mead" %}mead{% /term %} and {% term id="aquamarine" %}aquamarine{% /term %} are the {% term id="storm-islands" %}Storm Islands{% /term %} castle's. Below the tiles, {% ui key="client:overview.problems.title" /%} lists what the game refused the bot lately, in plain words, with the plugin that asked, how often and when. Each row is marked {% ui key="client:overview.errors.severe" /%}, {% ui key="client:overview.errors.notNow" /%} or {% ui key="client:overview.errors.other" /%}. The list keeps the last 100 kinds of refusal, also after the bot stops.
- {% ui key="common:nav.settings" /%}: the account name, the server, the game password, the event switch and the plugin list. Leave the password empty to keep the current one. {% ui key="client:drawer.openSettings" /%} next to a plugin takes you to its {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} page. Choose {% ui key="client:drawer.saveChanges" /%} when you are done.
- {% ui key="client:drawer.accountSettings" /%}: the pause between attacks, the **Daily attack limit**, which {% term id="time-skip" %}time skips{% /term %} the bot may use, the **Shutoff timer**, and whether the bot may read [gge-tracker.com timetables](#gge-tracker). This tab has its own save bar. The gear on the roster opens it directly.
- {% ui key="client:drawer.schedule" /%}: turn on {% ui key="client:schedule.toggle" /%} to let the bot work only inside the windows you set.
- {% ui key="client:nav.logs" /%}: this account's log lines, live. See [the Logs page](/war-room/logs/#account-logs).
- {% ui key="client:drawer.runHistory" /%}: the last 20 runs, with when each started, how long it ran and why it ended.

If you change the game password, the server, the event switch or which plugins are on, a running bot signs in again. A change to a plugin's options reaches the running bot without a new sign-in.

## Use gge-tracker.com timetables {% #gge-tracker %}

gge-tracker.com is a community website. Goodgame does not run it. It lists when each {% term id="fortress" %}fortress{% /term %} and Storm fort can be attacked again. With your permission, the Fortress and Storm forts plugins read those times instead of scanning the map. Your bot then finds targets all over the {% term id="kingdom" %}kingdom{% /term %}, not only near your castle.

Both boxes are on the account's {% ui key="client:drawer.accountSettings" /%} tab. Both are off until you tick them.

- **Use gge-tracker.com timetables**: the bot asks the site for your game server's timetables. It sends only the name of your game server, for example IN1.
- **Include my player name**: this box shows under the first one. The bot also sends your player name. The fortress times then include your own wait after each of your hits. Without your name, the site gives the times for every player.

The bot never sends your stats, your attacks or your account details. Only GGE Command's own server reads the site, once for all players on the same game server.

The site's times are a hint. Your bot still checks each target in the game before it attacks. If the site can't be read, the bot scans the map as before.

{% settings plugin="ggeTracker" /%}

## Remove an account {% #remove-account %}

Tick the account's box in the roster, then choose {% ui key="common:action.remove" /%} and confirm.

{% aside type="caution" id="remove-is-final" %}
Removing an account stops its bot and deletes its settings. You cannot undo it.
{% /aside %}

## Find anything with the command palette {% #command-palette %}

Press **⌘K** on a Mac, or **Ctrl+K** on other computers. You can also choose {% ui key="ui:palette.trigger" /%} in the header. On a phone, open your account menu and choose {% ui key="ui:palette.open" /%}.

Type a few letters. The {% term id="command-palette" %}palette{% /term %} finds:

- {% ui key="ui:palette.group.pages" /%}: every page in the sidebar.
- {% ui key="ui:palette.group.accounts" /%}: your game accounts. Choose one to open its panel.
- {% ui key="ui:palette.group.plugins" /%}: each plugin that has settings, once per account. Choose one to open its module page with that account picked.
- {% ui key="ui:palette.group.language" /%}: every language of the app.
- {% ui key="ui:palette.group.session" /%}: {% ui key="ui:nav.signOut" /%}.

Every word you type must match, and accents don't matter. Use the arrow keys to move, Enter to open and Esc to close.
